    "name": "Tropea onion",
    "description": "<p>Tropea onions, also known as Cipolle Rosse di Tropea, are a specialty of the Calabria region in Italy. They are known for their sweetness, aroma, and light flavor, which makes them ideal for eating raw in salads. The onions have a delicate herbal taste and are neither sour nor pungent. Their signature sweet taste comes from a reduced amount of pyruvic acid, which allows the natural sugars to dominate the flavor. When cooked, they caramelize beautifully.&nbsp;</p><br /><br />",
